abstract: >-
  FreeFem++ script that solves the two-dimensional sine-Gordon equation in a Y junction of three branches, with a
  homogeneous Neumann condition on the boundary, by quadratic Lagrange finite elements and a three-level scheme in time,
  implicit in the Laplacian and explicit in the sine, which keeps the energy. It computes a kink of speed 0.96 that
  crosses the fork and splits into two kinks, one in each upper branch, and writes the solution and the energy in each
  branch.
